---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Japan Living Edit, an independent English-language editorial website covering Japanese living ideas for international readers."
  pathname="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>An independent editorial view on everyday living from Japan.</h1>
    <p>
      Japan Living Edit is a Japan-based independent editorial website publishing
      English-language content for international readers, with a primary focus on
      readers in the United States.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="text-block">
    <p>
      The site covers Japanese products and everyday living ideas across organization,
      small-space living, kitchen tools and coffee. It is not an official website for
      any brand, retailer or affiliate program.
    </p>
    <p>
      The editorial goal is simple: explain what makes certain objects, routines and
      home ideas useful, calm and practical for real daily life.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <p>
      Coverage is chosen editorially, with attention to practical value, thoughtful
      design, efficient use of space and usefulness in everyday life. When it can be
      reasonably evaluated, durability is part of the conversation, but we do not make
      broad durability claims about products we have not used or inspected closely.
    </p>
    <p>
      Japan Living Edit is especially interested in distinctive Japanese approaches to
      organization and living: small adjustments, compact tools and quiet systems that
      help a home work better without feeling overdesigned.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      Inclusion on the site does not imply sponsorship, endorsement or an official
      relationship. Future commercial relationships should be disclosed clearly, and
      products should not receive positive coverage simply because an affiliate
      relationship exists.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some articles may be explanatory guides or editorial notes rather than hands-on
      reviews. When a product has not been personally tested, the article should avoid
      presenting it as a tested recommendation.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
